  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "* Added EnableAutoResumeDownload option to automatically resume downloads from existing .download files using saved metadata.\n            * Added IBinarySerializer interface and JsonBinarySerializer for serializing/deserializing download package resume metadata (replaced BsonSerializer).\n            * Added Serializer property on AbstractDownloadService to expose the inner binary serializer for external use.\n            * Added ArrayPool-based memory management in Packet and ChunkDownloader to reduce GC pressure and improve performance.\n            * Added synchronous Write method and ReadAsync(Memory) overload to ConcurrentStream.\n            * Added ForceFlushRelease in ConcurrentPacketBuffer to prevent deadlocks when the consumer (Watcher) crashes.\n            * Added proper disposal of remaining packets in ConcurrentPacketBuffer to return rented buffers to ArrayPool.\n            * Added [JsonIgnore] attributes to computed/runtime properties in Chunk, DownloadPackage, and ConcurrentStream for correct serialization.\n            * Added FileExistPolicy to control how existing destination files are handled.\n            * Added DownloadFileExtension to use a temporary extension during download, making in-progress files easy to identify (renamed to the final name on completion).\n            * Fixed IsMomentumError to recursively check InnerException, fixing retry logic for nested exceptions.\n            * Fixed live streaming data corruption by copying buffer data before returning it to ArrayPool.\n            * Fixed ConcurrentStream.DisposeAsync to properly await the watcher task before disposing the stream.\n            * Fixed ConcurrentStream.FlushAsync to check for faulted state and re-throw exceptions.\n            * Fixed an issue where the default Accept-Encoding header could cause corrupted downloads in range/multi-chunk mode (#206).\n            * Fixed completion/error handling: OnComplete could fire multiple times and the original exception was not always propagated to the caller.\n            * Fixed download from redirected URL (#31).\n            * Fixed download completion to trim resume metadata bytes from end of file stream.\n            * Reduced flush delay from 100ms to 20ms in DownloadPackage for faster completion.\n            * Removed unnecessary Task.Delay(100) after directory creation.",
